{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "title: \"Unit 2 Stretch\"\n",
        "author: \"Jonas Kennedy\"\n",
        "format: html\n",
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "Key things I think would be helpful to show in this class:\n",
        "\n",
        "- pivot and unpivot\n",
        "    - not necessary, but a good time to discuss implicit vs. explicit missing values\n",
        "- name.map(lambda function)\n",
        "- show facet wraps again"
      ],
      "id": "9303fab9"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "import polars as pl\n",
        "import numpy as np\n",
        "from lets_plot import *\n",
        "\n",
        "LetsPlot.setup_html(isolated_frame=True)\n",
        "\n",
        "df = pl.read_csv('https://byuistats.github.io/M335/data/rcw_reshape.csv')"
      ],
      "id": "3e8682d6",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "This data was collected from the first few semesters that the R&CW was run at the university level. It counts how many projects/entries were made in each semester from each department.\n",
        "\n",
        "Is the data in long or wide format? How can you tell? \n",
        "\n",
        "Convert it to wide with a `pivot()`:"
      ],
      "id": "83dab3a9"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "df_wide = df.pivot(on=\"Department\", values=\"Count\")\n",
        "\n",
        "df_wide"
      ],
      "id": "56a7d626",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Convert it back to long with unpivot():"
      ],
      "id": "990817a8"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "df_long = df_wide.unpivot(\n",
        "    index=[\"Year\", \"Semester\", \"Semester_Date\"],\n",
        "    variable_name=\"Department\",\n",
        "    value_name=\"Count\",\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "df_long"
      ],
      "id": "03c60958",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "### Discussion/Observation:\n",
        "\n",
        "* *How many rows does the new long format have? *\n",
        "\n",
        "42\n",
        "\n",
        "* *How does that compare with the original data? Why?*\n",
        "\n",
        "there are 7 more rows because we have null values in certain columns now\n",
        "\n",
        "*  *Discuss: When might you want to make implicit NA's explicit? Why would you not?*\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "\n",
        "# plotting\n",
        "\n",
        "Create a plot to look at how many projects were entered each semester by each department."
      ],
      "id": "d443635b"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "(ggplot(df_long, aes(x=\"Semester_Date\", y=\"Count\", color=\"Department\")) + geom_line())"
      ],
      "id": "9bc1444b",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "Do you see any issues with the plot? What do you think is causing the problem?\n",
        "\n",
        "Fix the issue and try plotting again.\n"
      ],
      "id": "026866f9"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "df_filled = df_long.with_columns(pl.col(\"Count\").fill_null(0))\n",
        "(ggplot(df_filled, aes(x=\"Semester_Date\", y=\"Count\", color=\"Department\")) + geom_line())"
      ],
      "id": "7e957b30",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "It's a bit busy, maybe we can break it out into small multiples. In other words a different plot for each Department. \n"
      ],
      "id": "1e69e59c"
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "departments = df_filled[\"Department\"].unique()\n",
        "for department in departments:\n",
        "    df_department = df_filled.filter(pl.col(\"Department\") == department)\n",
        "    (\n",
        "        ggplot(df_department, aes(x=\"Semester_Date\", y=\"Count\"))\n",
        "        + geom_line()\n",
        "        + labs(x=\"Semester Start Date\", title=department)\n",
        "    ).show()"
      ],
      "id": "d633a1e9",
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    }
  ],
